==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gem-pro|ang}} {{term/t|gem-pro|*hairaz}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|ang}} {{term/t|ine-pro|*kei-}}, {{term/t|ine-pro|*koi-}}. Cognate with Old High German {{term/t|goh|hēr}} (German {{term|hehr||august, holy|lang=de}}), Old Norse {{term|hárr||grey|lang=non}}, Gothic {{term|𐌷𐌰𐌹𐍃|tr=hais||torch|lang=got}}, Old Saxon {{term/t|osx|hēr}}. Non-Germanic cognates include Sanskrit {{term|केतु|tr=ketu||light, torch|lang=sa}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/hɑːɹ/|lang=ang}}

===Adjective===
{{ang-adj|head=hār}}

# Grey-haired, [[old]] and [[grey]], [[venerable]].

====Declension====
{{ang-decl-adj|hār}}

====Descendants====
* Middle English: {{l|enm|hore}}
** English: {{l/en|hoar}}

